    {"id":"INT-036","kind":"decision","text":"Operator confirms recovered Herdr workspaces; focus remaining work on migration and OpenCode/Codex/Herdr updates, reconsider the permanent Host helper, and revisit hibernation options afterward. Python and guests stay paused.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/current-session-focus.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-OPENCODE-HOST.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-035","kind":"requirement","text":"Refine INT-001 for signed Herdr Host: qualify a probe-only, journaled native unregister/promote/register operation for the replacement volume, preserving both signed bundles and running panes.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HERDR-RECOVERY.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HERDR-HOST-RECOVERY.plan.json"]},
    {"id":"INT-032","kind":"decision","text":"Pause all further Python environment updates and live activation for a separate session; preserve completed deliveries and rollback evidence.","disposition":"deferred","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/session-recovery-reopened.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-033","kind":"requirement","text":"Reopen exact-session recovery after empty home screens contradict prior identity-only verification; recover affected idle panes with positive conversation evidence, preserve new work and investigate reconnect behavior.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HERDR-RECOVERY.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/session-recovery-reopened.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-034","kind":"decision","text":"Resume hibernation qualification after session recovery and continue remaining non-Python host and coding-harness work; activation requires durable exact sleep/wake evidence.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HIBERNATION.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/session-recovery-reopened.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-001","kind":"requirement","text":"Verify and restore external-state tools after storage replacement, preserving exact conversations and layout.","disposition":"open","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/EXTERNAL-STATE.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HERDR-RECOVERY.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/GUESTS.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-002","kind":"constraint","text":"Preserve histories, credentials, archives, failed attempts and new V2 work; retain intentional redundant PPC DVC omissions.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-003","kind":"constraint","text":"Manage durable setup and external-state routing through chezmoi; verify redundancy before retiring installation ownership. Native updates replace custom updater ownership only after qualification.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-UPDATES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-004","kind":"requirement","text":"Update host tools and Python patch releases while preserving minor-version pins and proving relocated state works.","disposition":"open","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HOST-TOOLS.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/PYTHON-UPGRADES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-005","kind":"requirement","text":"Upgrade non-production Python environments only after candidate compatibility and runtime qualification.","disposition":"open","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/PYTHON-UPGRADES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-006","kind":"constraint","text":"Exclude enterprise-seo-tools and all production environments; preserve SDS GKE and shared production inputs.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-007","kind":"requirement","text":"Keep browser MCPs disconnected by default and manually connectable; restore Tab next-agent and Shift+Tab previous-agent.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md","docs/specs/opencode_control_plane/features/manual-browser-and-agent-keys.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-008","kind":"requirement","text":"Qualify an existing OpenCode-only hibernator for fifteen-minute idle unfocused sessions, preserving exact conversation identity and excluding working focused or blocked sessions.","disposition":"deferred","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HIBERNATION.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-009","kind":"decision","text":"Draft and exact scroll-position loss are accepted for hibernation; prefer official Herdr integration.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-010","kind":"decision","text":"Restarts are authorized with recovery preservation; native permission boundaries and exact launch consent remain enforced.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-011","kind":"requirement","text":"Complete original V2 delivery through its existing Initiative, defining fresh provisioning admission without replaying completed migration.","disposition":"open","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/DELIVERY-CLOSURE.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/GUESTS.md","docs/initiatives/opencode-rolling-stable/MANIFEST.json"]},
    {"id":"INT-012","kind":"decision","text":"Operator approved dotfiles host ownership, dotfiles-ai runtime ownership and per-project Python ownership; serialize shared writers.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/README.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/WORKSTREAMS.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-013","kind":"requirement","text":"Use native OpenCode updates on the invoked platform only; supported native installation owns executable updates and chezmoi preserves state routing without downgrade or executable shadowing.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-UPDATES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-014","kind":"decision","text":"Replace custom Codex updater ownership with a supported per-platform native installation after proving existing external state and configuration survive; supersede the earlier custom-updater-only requirement.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-UPDATES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-015","kind":"constraint","text":"Qualify install, native update, restart and chezmoi reapply against the same external state and exact resumable conversations before retiring old runtime ownership.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-UPDATES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-016","kind":"decision","text":"Prepare durable Discovery artifacts before compaction and delegate ownership-disjoint work using native subagents where exposed and permitted; primary retains integration and live deployment ownership.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/WORKSTREAMS.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-017","kind":"requirement","text":"Complete all previously scoped upgrades and migrations; hibernation is explicitly deferred until the rest is complete and must be surfaced then.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/WORKSTREAMS.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/DELIVERY-CLOSURE.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HIBERNATION.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-018","kind":"decision","text":"Upgrade all installed managed packages and applications, not just named session tools; resolve retired declarations and production coupling before activation.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HOST-TOOLS.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-019","kind":"decision","text":"Use latest stable Python dependencies allowed by existing project constraints, including allowed major versions; preserve Python minor pins and qualify runtime behavior before activation.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/PYTHON-UPGRADES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-020","kind":"decision","text":"Pause hibernation implementation and surface it after all other work completes; any integration repair or fork remains undecided until resumption.","disposition":"deferred","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HIBERNATION.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-021","kind":"decision","text":"Keep intentionally absent Loop and Shortcat removed; reconcile package declarations and receipts while preserving preferences.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/maintenance-follow-up.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-022","kind":"decision","text":"Keep the active standalone Google Cloud SDK as sole installer owner; qualify native updates and component preservation before retiring the Homebrew duplicate, and provide chezmoi bootstrap when absent.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HOST-TOOLS.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-023","kind":"decision","text":"Defer Linux x86_64 native-update activation; preserve its existing installation route and scope this transition to qualified macOS and Fedora ARM64 targets.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-UPDATES.md","docs/specs/dotfiles_ai_distribution/features/native-platform-updates.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-024","kind":"decision","text":"Defer all remaining guest work, including guest repairs, upgrades, runtime activation and fresh provisioning; continue host work without claiming guest completion.","disposition":"deferred","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/GUESTS.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/NATIVE-UPDATES.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-025","kind":"decision","text":"Defer the failed 1Password for Safari App Store update; continue all other host work.","disposition":"deferred","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/maintenance-follow-up.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-026","kind":"requirement","text":"Refine INT-004 shell-resolution work: select already-installed mise uv/uvx consistently in mac-mini Bash/Zsh login modes without activating unrelated runtimes, modifying project pins or installing during startup.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HOST-UV-SHELL.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-027","kind":"decision","text":"Operator confirms no additional host production consumers beyond enterprise-seo-tools and protected SDS workloads; retain those exclusions and verify shared-runtime coupling before upgrades.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/HOST-TOOLS.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-028","kind":"decision","text":"Defer content-evidence-workbench and search-taxonomy-lab upgrades until those projects are needed; preserve isolated qualification evidence and their existing live environments. Continue all other non-deferred work.","disposition":"deferred","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/PYTHON-UPGRADES.md","docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/maintenance-follow-up.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-029","kind":"decision","text":"Retire unused Aider instead of upgrading or changing its Python minor; preserve history and configuration.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/maintenance-follow-up.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-030","kind":"decision","text":"Retire unused host nginx, Laravel Valet and spatie/http-status-check; preserve site data and archive the obsolete global Composer tool installation/configuration.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/maintenance-follow-up.md"]},
    {"id":"INT-031","kind":"decision","text":"Accept seven reproduced pre-existing dotfiles-ai test failures for Python 3.13.16 test-environment activation only; retain rollback and revisit failures during host inventory and OpenCode cutover completion without waiving preservation guards.","disposition":"ready","artifacts":["docs/initiatives/ssd-toolchain-recovery/findings/maintenance-follow-up.md"]}
